  "body": "https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=8194\r\n\r\nCurrently moving the mouse cursor over text inside `<summary>` changes its cursor style to \"text\", the same style for regular (non-interactive) text. I find it a bit confusing. \r\n\r\nPeople may notice it is interactive by looking at the triangle beside it. But it may be great to make it more visible , like explicitly setting `cursor: default` or `pointer` on UA stylesheets.",
